WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.652
A pivot often requires aggregation If only one
source row maps

00:00:05.678 --> 00:00:11.282
to each output cell the reshape can preserve that
value directly But

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:16.493
if multiple source rows map to one cell PostgreSQL
needs an aggregate such as SUM

00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:22.156
COUNT MAX or AVG That aggregation changes the level

00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:24.959
of detail so it must be chosen deliberately
